<title>GERMANY: West German Sept adjusted unemployment rises.</title>
<headline>West German Sept adjusted unemployment rises.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Sep 96	  Aug 96	   Sep 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.748 million     2.779 million	2.488 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		2.851 million     2.817 million	2.599 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +34,000	 +32,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		8.9 pct	 9.0 pct	  8.1 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	152,613	 116,474	  101,267</p>
<p> Vacancies		   259,211	 274,150	  256,602</p>
<p> Change in number in wrk Jul 96	  Jun 96</p>
<p>				 unch	    -5,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
